Subject: [PATCH] projectM TV: smooth switches and blends on TV hardware

Changes for ProjectM TV (Android TV, NVIDIA SHIELD profiling), on top of 4.1.7:

- projectm_opengl_render_frame_fbo(): render into a caller-supplied framebuffer
  (same name as later projectM versions), so the app can render below the
  surface size and upscale.
- Framebuffer::SetSize() scales the old color contents into the new textures:
  a render size change no longer restarts every preset (almost all presets draw
  on top of their previous frame).
- Process-wide cache of linked program binaries (glGetProgramBinary /
  glProgramBinary), keyed by shader source, shared by all instances:
  projectm_opengl_program_cache_stats(). A second instance on a background
  thread links the next preset's programs, so the switch on the render thread
  no longer waits ~0.3-0.5 s per program in the driver's compiler.
- Shader: uniform locations looked up once per program, and glUseProgram only
  when a different program is bound (custom shapes bound the same program
  several times per instance, each time forcing the driver to revalidate).
- projectm_opengl_set_outgoing_preset_frame_divisor(): during a soft cut, the
  outgoing preset can render every n-th frame (its last frame is blended in
  between), halving its CPU cost when blends are CPU-bound.

